<title>BRAZIL: Most Brazil coffee coops report cooler night.</title>
<headline>Most Brazil coffee coops report cooler night.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian cooperatives and weather monitoring centers in most coffee areas reported cooler early morning temperatures on Friday than on the previous day.</p>
<p>Weather services are expecting below normal temperatures in the coffee areas over the coming days but no frosts are forecast.</p>
<p>Early morning/minimum temperatures in degrees Celsius on Friday and Thursday were as follows.</p>
<p>						FRIDAY, MAY 30    THURSDAY, MAY 29</p>
<p>  PARANA, Londrina			     12			10</p>
<p> PARANA, Cornelio Procopio		   16			14</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Marilia			    14			16</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Franca			     13			18</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Sao Sebastiao do Paraiso   9			15</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Pocos de Caldas		7			13</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
